{
    "about": "Our own grouping of Unicode's non-emoji special characters, built from UnicodeData.txt and Blocks.txt by tools/build-dataset.php. A character joins a group when its block is listed and its general category starts with one of the listed prefixes; `name` narrows by name. Controls, format and invisible characters, private use, surrogates, unassigned code points, separators and standalone combining marks are never included — they cannot be seen, and several are the raw material of text-smuggling attacks. `popular` is a hand-picked list. A rule may instead list `extra` code points (hex) to add by hand — the CJK ideographs and Hangul syllable used as currency signs, which Unicode names by rule rather than listing (`HEX=NAME` supplies the name).",
